    "title": "Interstate 10 around Beaumont seeing morning congestion - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kim Brent ,\n16 hours ago Here's the traffic update for Beaumont drivers on Wednesday night. (Kim Brent) Drivers heading to and through Beaumont will experience some major slowdowns this morning.\nTexas Department of Transportation live traffic reports are showing heavy congestion that builds just past College Street on Interstate 10 westbound, with the major glut of traffic slowing almost to a standstill per Waze app users between Sam's Club and Washington Boulevard.\nThose taking the on-ramp to U.S. 69 are also creeping their way through the turn, though they'll be picking up speed quickly once on the highway going south.\nRELATED: Homecoming parade will close some roads tonight in Beaumont\nThere is also the usual one-lane slowdown for those heading south on U.S. 69 between the interchange to I-10 east and Harrison Avenue.\nAnyone traveling east on the interstate coming toward Beaumont are also getting snarled in a major traffic jam, according to the TxDOT map and Waze reports. There is a stretch of very heavy traffic extending from North Fork Taylor Bayou to about a mile east of FM 365.\nThere haven't been any reports of accidents accounting for this morning's tie-ups, but the 10 mph or less you'll be doing through the congestion is going to tack some time onto this morning's drive.\nCheck back this afternoon for a preview of what to expect on the evening commute.\nSign up for Beaumont Enterprise newsletters here\nRead the original article on beaumontenterprise.com",
